## Conversation
Unattended monitor-and-fix loop for PR #15153. Maintainer rmccorm4 reviewed e2b2da7bd9 and left three inline comments: two P2 reference-validation defects and one P3 test-timeout request. This commit addresses all three.

## Actions
Reproduced both P2 findings against the walker before changing code: {"type":"object","$ref":"#/$defs/base","$defs":{"base":true}} and {"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"$ref":"#"} both returned Ok. Added validate_reference_closure: for a $ref sibling that is an object schema without local constraints, follow the target chain to the first target with its own constraints and require additionalProperties: false there. Removed the sibling-keyword early break from validate_reference_cycles so every direct $ref edge is followed; recursion through properties/items/anyOf children is still fine because those are separate nodes. Renamed the diagnostic to "direct reference cycles". Added a bounded() helper with a 10 s tokio timeout around send(), json(), and bytes() in the two strict-schema HTTP tests via post_json. Updated the guide sentence on references. Rebased onto upstream/main 373bc9f929 first (vllm-omni FastH3, no overlap). Verified 12 walker tests, 513 protocols::openai tests, clippy -D warnings on lib and test targets, fmt, docs lint, diff --check.

## Errors & Mistakes
None in this round.

## Dead Ends
Considered merging closure into validate_object by resolving targets during the BFS, but targets are only known after all nodes are indexed, so a post-pass over resolved targets was the smaller change.

## Hints for Future Agents
validate_reference_closure stops at the first target that has local constraints because validate_object already enforced additionalProperties: false on that node when it ran; only the final node's additionalProperties is checked directly for the constraint-free chain case. Nullable wrappers like {"type":["object","null"],"$ref":...} are object schemas and are checked too; the positive test covers that shape. The HTTP tests cannot run in this sandbox (socket bind denied); only compile and clippy were verified locally for that file.

## Codebase Discoveries
The harness client in lib/llm/tests/common/http_harness.rs is built without a timeout and is shared by four test binaries, so the bound was added in this file's post_json rather than the shared client to avoid changing other suites.

